From the tone of your post it sounds like you might be overemphasizing
combat and in particular melee.  I tend to wear gauntlets of power,
too, but not for the damage bonus, it's because I hate not having a
piece of gear due to encumberance.  Things like rings of inc accuracy
and increase damage rarely advance the hero toward ascending more than
walking past the obstacle, zapping with a wand of teleport, or if the
obstacle needs to be killed, zapping with a wand of death or cast
magic missile (etc.).

During the ascension run, on levels where teleport is allowed, just
wear a ring of teleport (and be LVL 17, IIRC) and teleport past any
monsters.  Why bother killing them?  If the Wizard shows up zap him
with a wand of death.  Same goes for the riders since they can not be
teleported away.  The other denizens on the Astral Plane can just be
teleported away or jumped past.
